{"step_index":91,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-07T06:32:06Z","input_tokens":3709,"cache_read_tokens":49383,"output_tokens":1256,"thinking":"All backend logic tests have passed. Authentication scenarios, including success (200) with session maintenance and failure (400, 401), are confirmed. Unauthorized API access is correctly rejected (401). Note creation with empty content is denied (400), and successful note creation returns (201). Note retrieval (200) and nonexistent note retrieval (404) function as expected, as do note updates (200), including rejection of updates with empty content (400) which preserves the original content and note deletions(200), with subsequent attempts to delete yielding 404 errors.\n\n\nSetting up the frontend structure, starting with the directory organization and essential configuration files.  Vite will be configured to proxy API requests to the backend. React components will be divided logically, with state and API requests managed separately within designated files.\n\nThe initial components will handle login (including error handling), a dashboard (displaying user information and a logout mechanism), and a request history view.\n\n\nFrontend directory structure is being established, starting with the creation of `monitor/frontend` and the initialization of `package.json`.  Considering using React 18 or 19 with Vite, and `@vitejs/plugin-react` due to the existing node.js and npm versions. Stable versions of `react`, `react-dom`, `vite`, and `@vitejs/plugin-react` will be installed.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"{\n  \"name\": \"monitor-frontend\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"version\": \"0.0.0\",\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"dev\": \"vite\",\n    \"build\": \"vite build\",\n    \"preview\": \"vite preview\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"react\": \"^18.3.1\",\n    \"react-dom\": \"^18.3.1\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@types/react\": \"^18.3.5\",\n    \"@types/react-dom\": \"^18.3.0\",\n    \"@vitejs/plugin-react\": \"^4.3.1\",\n    \"vite\": \"^5.4.2\"\n  }\n}\n","Description":"Create package.json for monitor/frontend","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"c:\\work\\mini-watch-day03-start\\monitor\\frontend\\package.json","toolAction":"Creating package.json","toolSummary":"Create frontend package.json"}}]}
